# Fincz Expense Tracker — Cursor Rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for the full project guide. This file contains Cursor-specific rules and quick hints.

---

## Project Identity

Angular 22 + Angular Material 22 + Dexie.js (IndexedDB) + SCSS + Angular Signals.
Offline-first — no backend, no API calls. All data in browser IndexedDB.
Package manager: **pnpm only**.

---

## Code Style Rules

- All components are standalone (`standalone: true`)
- Use `inject()` for dependency injection, not constructor parameters
- State is managed with Angular `signal()` and `computed()` — not RxJS BehaviorSubject
- All component styles are written inline in the `styles: [...]` array — no separate .scss files for components
- Global utilities and CSS variables are in `src/styles.scss`
- Use `async/await`, not `.then()` chains
- Mobile-first CSS: base styles for mobile, `@media (min-width: 768px)` for desktop overrides

---

## Naming Conventions

- Files: `kebab-case.component.ts`, `kebab-case.service.ts`, `kebab-case.model.ts`
- Classes: `PascalCase`
- Signals: private `myDataSignal`, public readonly as `myData = computed(...)`
- CSS classes: `kebab-case`

---

## Do NOT

- Run `pnpm run start` or `ng serve`
- Use `npm` or `yarn`
- Create NgModules
- Use `window` / `document` directly (SSR will break — use `isPlatformBrowser`)
- Insert duplicate category names (unique constraint in Dexie)
- Change DB schema without incrementing the version number

---

## CSS Variables to Use

```scss
var(--primary-color)    // #2563eb — blue, expenses
var(--accent-color)     // #059669 — green, income
var(--bg-color)         // #f8fafc — page background
var(--surface-color)    // #ffffff — card background
var(--text-main)        // #0f172a
var(--text-muted)       // #64748b
var(--border-color)     // #e2e8f0
var(--radius-md)        // 16px — for cards
var(--radius-sm)        // 8px — for inputs
var(--shadow-sm)
var(--safe-area-bottom) // iOS safe area
```

---

## Reusable Utilities

```html
<!-- Standard card -->
<div class="m3-card">...</div>

<!-- Material icon -->
<span class="material-symbols-outlined">icon_name</span>
```

